  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "484e830c-7613-4ccf-b5a2-f4f434fb2c9d",
    "name": "Quix Cloud HTTP APIs Definitions Parameter Data API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "OpenAPI 3.0 description of the HTTP (REST) surfaces of Quix Cloud: the Streaming Writer API for publishing time-series parameter data, events, and definitions into Quix topics, and the account-wide Portal API for managing workspaces, topics, and deployments.\n\nThe Streaming Reader API is delivered exclusively over a Microsoft SignalR hub (WebSockets / Long Polling) and is therefore modeled separately in the companion AsyncAPI document at asyncapi/quix-asyncapi.yml, not here.\n\nAll endpoints authenticate with a Quix Personal Access Token (PAT) supplied as an `Authorization: Bearer <PAT>` header. The Streaming Writer API base host is environment-specific (`writer-{environmentId}.cloud.quix.io`); the Portal API is account-wide (`portal-api.platform.quix.io`). Endpoint paths are documented by Quix; per-environment Swagger/OpenAPI references are available from the Quix portal under Settings > APIs and tokens.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Quix Support",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
